+/// Removes the identity of the entry function from a callee key reached from
+/// a checking root (see [`identity_semantic_instance_key`]), so that equal
+/// work reached from different entry functions shares one instance.
+///
+/// Such a key names the entry function in places that do not affect the
+/// callee's analysis:
+/// - a provider's `uses` source site, an identity token that callers resolve
+///   back to their own effect arguments through the callee's effect
+///   environment; it is re-rooted at the callee's own `uses` parameter for
+///   that slot. Contract fields and root providers name one object wherever
+///   they occur and are kept;
+/// - a provider's provenance, which names the caller's binding;
+/// - the proof environment, whose normalization scope only selects an ingot
+///   and whose assumptions may constrain parameters the key never mentions.
+///
+/// Providers the caller supplies from its own locals already carry the
+/// callee's source and keep their provenance. Keys reached from code
+/// generation roots are left unchanged, as are keys where two providers share
+/// a `uses` source (re-rooting would split an alias).
