@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Add `std::evm::checksum_address` for ERC-55 checksummed address formatting. Expand regression coverage of the existing `core::num::isqrt` across power-of-two and maximum-square boundaries.
diff --git a/newsfragments/+borrowck-entry-instance-sharing.performance.md b/newsfragments/+borrowck-entry-instance-sharing.performance.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..aa8291a9f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/newsfragments/+borrowck-entry-instance-sharing.performance.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+`fe check` no longer borrow checks a function once for every entry point that reaches it. Functions called from several entry functions through a trait-keyed effect such as `uses (ops: mut RawOps)`, or from several receive arms of the same contract, now share one checked instance. Checking a Seaport port with many entry points went from about 6.5 to 2.5 minutes.
diff --git a/newsfragments/+dyn-array-composite-elements.feature.md b/newsfragments/+dyn-array-composite-elements.feature.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..acf3c6c01
--- /dev/null
+++ b/newsfragments/+dyn-array-composite-elements.feature.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+`DynArray::get` now works for every ABI element type, including multi-word static structs and tuples and dynamic elements such as `Bytes`. `MemVec` accepts any static ABI element type. The new `std::abi::dyn_array_from([..])` builds a `DynArray` from a fixed array of any element type (for example a `bytes[]`), and `std::abi::canonical_dyn_array` re-encodes a decoded array in canonical layout.
